    "turn_text": "is, you know, you got true believers, you got grifters. And, you know, I talk about the E.L. in this book, which somebody said, Randy McBride should play the expedition later in this book. you know, what I'm looking at is that I paid to do this. I think my wife and I paid $2,000 apiece to go on this Bigfoot expedition in a public park. Or we had some reservists, he said he was a military reservist using a four foot stick to say, this is how you tell the gate of a Bigfoot from foot foot to foot, what? You know, so we just had some weird things happening there. But again, I think it comes down to I just don't know, just when you're talking to the Bigfoot individuals, and I know I'm having a segue here, when you're talking to these individuals, and if you prove something without a shout, you're like, this can't happen because of this, they automatically get angry. And I saw that a real anger. I mean, we're talking about Bigfoot, right? You know, I had one individual tell me, you got to have faith. No, I don't. Like, no, actually, you're talking about an eight foot tall being that smells like, that can actually, by the way, I don't know if you know this, Bigfoot can also emit a very specific odor to drive you away, sort of like a skunk, like the world's biggest skunk. You believe that's happening and he throws rocks at you and he tears off the heads of squirrels and puts them on your porch to tell you he loves you. And so I'm just supposed to take that as faith. No, tell me why Bigfoot rips off the squirrels. I really want to know. Right? Well, we don't know. It's just we think it's a sign of love.",
