  {
    "episode_id": 46426,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/6/46426.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 248,
    "turn_text": "I mean, I listen, I mean, we're to a point, I mean, I make liquor for God's sakes, Matt. I mean, it's a controlled substance right here. It's a good one. But I think that's why I'm saying, listen, this is ridiculous. And people are like, well, Denver, it's a gateway drug. I had something on the floor telling me like, Denver, you're so full of crap. You just want kids to get on heroin. And you want them to get on cocaine. And you want them to smoke crack. And I'm like, no, man. I just don't want a guy who has a joint. you know, to go to jail for something that is no, and I know this is scientifically, it is not worse than what we're drinking now. It's just not.",
