    "turn_idx": 252,
    "turn_text": "I thought, I thought that just my incredible charisma and good looks, you know, I'm sort of the chubby Tom Cruise of Congress, right? But I, I honestly thought with policy and trying to, and I kept telling people, you're allowed to live the way you want to live. My job is to protect, I can't say I'm a me evangelical Christian. I'm not. That's a lie. But I also can't say that I think that you guys should direct how people live. That can't happen. You know? It can't happen, Matt. And that cost because I refused. So here's what happened. The committee member said, hey, if you pay us, you're not going to have an opponent. I refused to pay off the committee members and I committed the ultimate Senate of officiating a same-sex wedding because I refused to pay off these people for graft too because they're grifters. And, you know, if there's something I despise, right, is this sort of this underbelly of grifting that's just the person that they want to latch on to or the fact that I refuse to pay them knowing that they would never have any audience with me. It's very difficult when you call me a baby-killing sodomite or call me a fag lover, right, or say that I'm the tool of the antichrist. That's what I was called. My wife was called the spawn of Satan, and I figured with me being the tool of the anti-Christ and her being the spawn of Satan, we're the new power couple of Virginia,",
