    "turn_text": "am, because you know, it wasn't a politics man. I mean, you've had that discussion, you know, somebody's like, I'm really happy with you sometimes, and sometimes you don't want to throat punch it, you know? I think a lot of it has to do with my background in the military and what I saw overseas. I'm a China hawk because I've seen what China's done. I've been in South America. I've seen what they've done as far as the debt trap they're putting countries into. So I have this bizarre sort of, I'm so libertarian on the social side like I don't give a rat. you know, but when it comes to sort of us playing in sort of the world hegemonic games, I'm like, we better or we're going to be fighting wars on our soil. And it's sort of the counter-terrorism slant, too. And I love having those discussions in a very positive way, and I do, right? Whether it would be with a Justin or with a Massey or with the people that I talk to somebody like, Denver, you're so full of crap, man, on Faison. I'm like, yeah, but there's this. You know and you know Jim Jordan and even Jim came up with stuff and so I've always been very Specific about how I argue that and I think they appreciated that honesty right I never hid But so I'm almost like this. I don't know what I am man You know I just want to do what's best for the Americans at that time based on whatever we have in front of us And it I don't know if that makes me cut out for politics or not and and and I don't know if I am I mean to be honest with you I",
